WEBVTT

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:02.020
Daisuke!

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.490
Jinko!

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:05.440
<b>The Regular Meet Thus Far</b>

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:05.440
The regular meet thus far!

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:09.400
The regular meet's finally underway!

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.070
It's bein' held at the secret flower garden 
known as Asagaoka Girls' High School.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.680
Round 1 was a paper quiz!

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:18.910
<b>1st   Buzou High School 
Sasajima Gakuto</b>

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.970
Sasajima-senpai from Buzou 
High School placed first.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.040
<b>1st   Buzou High School 
Sasajima Gakuto</b>

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:21.040
<b>2nd   Kaijou High School 
Ohkura Kunimitsu</b>

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:21.650
Kaijou High School's President 
Ohkura placed second.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:27.510
And those who ranked third, fourth, 
fifth, sixth, seventh, eighth, ninth,

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:23.210
<b>3rd   Miyaura High School 
Ashiya Yousuke</b>

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:23.960
<b>4th   Kaijou High School 
Konoe Haruomi</b>

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:24.670
<b>5th   Leoneil High School 
Tozuka Koutarou</b>

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:25.460
<b>6th   Kannami University 
High School 
Shibuya Hiroki</b>

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:26.210
<b>7th   Kaijou High School 
Shibata Masaru</b>

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:26.960
<b>8th   Kannami University 
High School 
Hanabusa Minoru</b>

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:27.670
<b>9th   Kaijou High School 
Hosokawa Atsuyoshi</b>

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:30.420
and tenth advanced to 
the third round as seeds.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:28.630
<b>10th   Miyaura High School 
Mikuriya Chisato</b>

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.380
<b>Seeded for Round 3</b>

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.380
Round 2 was a "fastest finger" showdown.

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:35.630
The Fukami x Yagi pairin'
 won their group easy.

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:38.810
In the followin' group, the 
Maruyama x Inoue pairin'...

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:40.650
failed.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:45.350
The Kumada x Hirosue pairin' 
went through instead.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:48.750
Sure, I lost, but I have no regrets!

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:51.170
Yep, yep. You did jus' great, pardner!

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:54.360
And now, it's finally Shiki-kun's turn!

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:59.530
<i>It's not just the people answering 
that think about the questions.</i>

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:03.300
<i>The people who write the 
questions think hard about them,</i>

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.680
<i>and a lot of detailed planning 
goes into coming up with them.</i>

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:10.370
<i>If I can read into that and understand it...</i>

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:16.740
Well, it's time for the next 
group to start, Onee-sama.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:21.470
Which pairing will advance to Round 3?

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:05.410
<b>Question 9: "High Road x Low Road"</b>

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:10.310
<i>This regular meet holds 
special meaning for me.</i>

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:13.580
The regular meet in June is up next.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:14.350
Huh?

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:15.560
Revenge!

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:17.620
I'm telling you...

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:19.510
to do quiz bowl!

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:24.220
<i>To get revenge on Mikuriya-kun,</i>

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:26.430
<i>I have to win this round</i>

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:29.150
<i>and face Mikuriya-kun in Round 3.</i>

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:34.100
Have you all drawn your cards?

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:36.310
<i>So, who am I paired with?</i>

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:38.210
Oh, we have the same card!

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:40.150
Hi there, partner.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:43.140
Oh... I'm Koshiyama, 
first-year at Buzou High School.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:44.110
I know.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.430
Hey, isn't that...

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:50.330
It's the kid we ran into by 
the vending machine at lunch.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:53.230
I'm Sonohara. I'm a third-year 
at Sekigawata Middle School.

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:56.100
I'm new to our club.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.550
Wait, are you...

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:01.520
<i>Man, he figured it out already?</i>

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:04.670
...the Asagaoka club president's 
younger brother? Sonohara, right?

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:06.920
<i>Oh, that's what he meant?</i>

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:10.520
That's right. I'm her brother, Akira.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:12.530
He's adorable!

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:15.270
President Sonohara's 
younger brother, he said!

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:18.400
<i>I've seen Koshiyama's partner 
somewhere before...</i>

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.530
The last group has been decided.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:24.700
Coincidentally, all the middle
 schoolers are in this one!

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.470
We will now begin.

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:31.080
Question.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.910
In America, major league 
baseball is comprised of—

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:37.540
<i>The little squirts are fast!</i>

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:41.900
The winners of the right to answer are 
Ohara-kun, Kaijou Middle School first-year,

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:44.050
and Sekigawata Middle School 
first-year, Sasaki-kun.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:45.690
American League.

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:46.810
Correct.

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:48.310
National League.

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:49.240
Correct.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:52.390
<b>Q: In America, major league baseball is comprised of 
two leagues: what and what?  A. American, National</b>

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:52.390
<i>They were in elementary school 
until just a few months ago!</i>

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:54.730
<i>I know how fast Sasaki-kun is on the buzzer.</i>

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:57.100
<i>And a middle schooler from 
Kaijou beat him to the punch...</i>

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:01.320
<b>Group</b>

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:01.320
Mouri x Ohara

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:01.320
Sonohara x 
Koshiyama

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:01.320
Sasaki x Ima

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:01.320
Mukai x Yasuura

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:00.030
<i>Good thing those two aren't a pair.</i>

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:01.320
So...

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:04.950
The first pair to get five 
"Right" marks wins, right?

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:08.790
Right. And if we answer correctly 
as a pair, we get three "Rights."

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:11.400
But we can only answer
wrong once, so be careful.

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:14.410
<i>It's too early to take risks, isn't it?</i>

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:17.300
<i>What to do? What should I do?</i>

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:20.340
<i>If I try to buzz at the determining point,</i>

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:22.130
<i>I think it'll be too late.</i>

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:24.800
<i>I need to be...</i>

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:26.500
<i>faster!</i>

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.290
Question.

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:31.830
A classic string quartet uses four inst—

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:36.480
Koshiyama-kun of Buzou has 
won the right to answer first.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:37.810
<i>The category is music...</i>

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:39.980
Second is Mukai-kun of Miyaura.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:43.440
<i>I buzzed reflexively
 because Koshiyama did!</i>

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:46.210
<i>The string instruments used 
in a string quartet...</i>

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:48.600
Four to choose from...

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:52.080
<i>If the question is really 
that straightforward...</i>

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:54.180
<i>Which two are the answers?</i>

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:57.460
<i>There are four, but the question is easy.</i>

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.300
<i>The instruments in a string quartet</i>

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:03.830
<i>are the first violin, second 
violin, cello, and viola.</i>

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:07.090
<i>What sticks out is that two of 
them are the same instrument.</i>

00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:11.840
<i>No matter how I look at it, 
the question has to be,</i>

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:15.870
<i>"a classic string quartet uses four 
instruments: two violins plus what and what?"</i>

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:17.980
<i>Mukai-kun buzzed second.</i>

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:22.060
Three, two...

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:24.590
<i>Which means the answer I should give...</i>

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:26.360
<i>is this one!</i>

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:27.860
Cello.

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:30.280
<i>Just listen to that confidence.</i>

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:33.060
Correct.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.950
Mukai-kun, the other answer, please.

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:40.000
O-Okay... Violin!

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:42.290
<i>That was all I could think of!</i>

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:45.300
<b>Q: A classic string quartet uses four instruments: 
first violin, second violin, what, and what?  A: Cello, viola</b>

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:45.300
Sorry. The second answer was "viola."

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:48.660
<i>Sorry, I left the harder answer for you.</i>

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:52.000
The Koshiyama x Sonohara pairing 
earns one "Right" mark,

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:52.140
<b>Group</b>

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:52.140
Mouri x Ohara

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:52.140
Sonohara x 
Koshiyama

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:52.140
Sasaki x Ima

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:52.140
Mukai x Yasuura

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:55.060
and the Yasuura x Mukai pairing 
now has one "Wrong" mark.

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:57.340
That first-year from Buzou is pretty good.

00:06:57.340 --> 00:07:00.100
Sasajima must be training him well.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:02.650
Nah, I bet that answer 
was just a wild guess.

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:06.230
Wow! I can't believe you 
figured it out from just that!

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:07.170
Yeah...

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:12.360
But there was really no way to be absolutely 
sure until the two violins were read.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:13.960
I wanted the right to answer,

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:16.870
so I got a bit hasty and buzzed 
before the determining point,

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:18.450
but I'm glad I still got it right.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:22.010
Hm... Determining point, huh?

00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:24.040
Okay, then, next time...

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:25.650
I'll buzz in.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:27.080
Huh?

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:28.860
Question.

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:30.300
In th—

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:37.560
It lit up!

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:41.270
<i>Finger slipped? No...</i>

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:43.520
<i>He took a dive on purpose.</i>

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:47.270
<i>Hey, that's right! She'll keep 
reading the question!</i>

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:50.740
In the name of the wireless LAN 
technology, "Wi-Fi," the "Wi" and—

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:54.870
Th-The right to answer first goes 
to Sonohara-kun of Sekigawata.

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:57.410
Second is Sasaki-kun of Sekigawata.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:59.770
<i>Everyone was so distracted 
by Akira-kun's buzz,</i>

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:03.080
<i>it slowed down our reactions 
to buzz in second.</i>

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:04.050
Let's see... What was the question again?

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:06.030
Oh, Wi-Fi, right?

00:08:06.030 --> 00:08:08.170
<i>Why is he waiting until now to think?</i>

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:07.720
The "Wi" is...

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:09.380
Wireless.

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:10.130
Correct.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:11.840
<i>O-Of course!</i>

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.110
The second answer, Sasaki-kun, please.

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:15.720
Fidelity.

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:18.220
<b>Q: In the name of the wireless LAN technology, "Wi-Fi," the 
"Wi" and "Fi" stand for what and what?  A: Wireless, Fidelity</b>

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:16.920
Correct.

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:20.470
Can people really answer questions 
just by hearin' one word?

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:24.720
I don't think one word is enough for 
anyone to determine the answer.

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:26.440
Is it like Mikuriya with "Why climb"?

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:28.280
I don't think so.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:30.470
He buzzed in early,

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:34.110
but he was still able to hear the question 
until it reached a determining point.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:37.320
<b>Group</b>

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:37.320
Mouri x Ohara

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:37.320
Sonohara x 
Koshiyama

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:37.320
Sasaki x Kon

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:37.320
Mukai x Yasuura

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:37.320
He found the flaw in the 
rule set of this round.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:41.390
<i>But even if you know the answers, it's 
not easy to do something that risky.</i>

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:42.540
Akira-kun...

00:08:43.030 --> 00:08:45.400
You knew you'd hear more of the 
question until the second buzz.

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:46.750
That's why you buzzed, right?

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:49.710
Because you knew no one would 
buzz before that point.

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:51.210
S-Seriously?

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:53.340
That little brat!

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:55.230
That's right.

00:08:55.230 --> 00:08:57.680
I never could've guessed it 
from just that one word.

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:01.640
No one else is going to buzz before 
that "point" thing comes along, right?

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:06.650
So it'll work out the same way 
whenever the first person buzzes in.

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:11.400
We get to hear more of the question until 
someone else buzzes in second, anyway.

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:16.360
Besides, there haven't been any questions yet 
in this round where both answers were hard.

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:17.830
<i>He's right.</i>

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:19.910
<i>Since we only have to 
get one of two answers,</i>

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:23.480
<i>all the questions so far 
have been relatively easy.</i>

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:25.100
<i>He calculated all this?</i>

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:27.290
Super successful, wouldn't you say?

00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:31.130
So no matter when the first person 
buzzes, it ends up the same?

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:33.230
I didn't realize the 
rules had that loophole.

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:35.060
Don't be fooled, idiot.

00:09:35.060 --> 00:09:35.670
What?

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:39.640
It was a dick move that 
only works the first time.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:42.390
You and Inoue-kun took a 
dive and guessed wrong.

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:46.920
Mukai's finger slipped when Koshiyama-kun 
buzzed early, and he guessed wrong, too.

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:50.580
They all tried to estimate when the others 
would be more cautious about buzzing,

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:52.430
taking advantage of a 
psychological weakness.

00:09:52.430 --> 00:09:52.980
Yuck...

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:55.570
That won't work a second time.

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:57.410
Question.

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:58.270
A—

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:02.140
Did the Ohara x Mouri pairing 
buzz in accidentally?

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:03.730
Why'd you buzz in?!

00:10:03.730 --> 00:10:04.910
Why did <i>you</i>?!

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:08.080
Since both are unable to answer, they get 
two "Wrong" marks and are disqualified.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:10.230
Yes, I love it! What a blast!

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:12.460
Uh, Akira-kun...

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:15.550
You've gotta be adventurous 
or it's no fun, right?

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:17.220
It's a game, after all.

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:20.690
<i>What's with that kid?</i>

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:22.180
<i>He's creeping me out.</i>

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:24.680
President Sonohara?

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:26.590
Please do not talk among yourselves.

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:29.290
Continuing to do so will lead 
to instant disqualification.

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:30.400
Aw...

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:34.650
Okay. Sorry.

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:37.820
Um, as for the current scores...

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:42.660
The remaining Sonohara x Koshiyama 
pairing and Sasaki x Kon pairing are tied.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:46.120
<b>Group</b>

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:46.120
Mouri x Ohara | Sonohara x Koshiyama | Sasaki x Kon | Mukai x Yasuura

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:46.120
The Yasuura x Mukai pair has one "Wrong" 
mark, putting them in a tight spot.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:48.370
So if they answer right as a pair...

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:49.870
They get three "Right" marks.

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:53.620
So if Shiki-kun and his partner answer 
right as a pair, they can win?

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:57.380
Right, but I have a bad feeling 
about where this is going...

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:03.710
<i>Get it together! Just do 
this like I always do!</i>

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:06.310
<i>I won't lose to a senior who 
treats this like a joke!</i>

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:08.070
<i>I have to focus!</i>

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:10.540
Question.

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:13.730
The Roman god of erotic 
love, Cupid, had two—

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:13.730
<i>Yes!</i>

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:14.730
<i>That's a classic!</i>

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.250
<i>I was too slow!</i>

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:17.220
Golden arrows!

00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:18.470
Correct.

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:19.770
Lead arrows!

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:20.950
<b>Q: The Roman god of erotic love, Cupid, had two types 
of arrows: what and what?  A: Golden arrows, lead arrows</b>

00:11:19.770 --> 00:11:20.950
Correct.

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:22.300
Question.

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:26.290
The Russian author Turgenev said 
humanity could be divided into two—

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:27.240
<i>I'm first!</i>

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:28.500
<i>Don't rush.</i>

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:30.330
Hamlet types!

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:31.030
Correct.

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:32.340
Don Quixote types!

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:33.170
<b>Q: The Russian author Turgenev said humanity could be divided into two 
types: the "what" type and the "what" type?  A: Hamlet type, Don Quixote type</b>

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:33.170
Correct.

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:35.380
<b>Group</b>

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:35.380
Mouri x Ohara

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:35.380
Sonohara x 
Koshiyama

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:35.380
Sasaki x Kon

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:35.380
Mukai x Yasuura

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:35.380
The Sasaki x Kon pairing needs one more to win!

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:37.880
Will the next question decide the contest?

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:38.840
<i>I got this!</i>

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:41.800
<i>Even if I win the right to answer,</i>

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:43.470
Sonohara x 
Koshiyama

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:43.470
Sasaki x Kon

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:45.010
<i>Sasaki-kun will most likely 
be the other one to buzz in.</i>

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:47.160
<i>I can't stop him by myself.</i>

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:51.440
<i>Mukai-kun's pairing has one "Wrong" 
mark, so they'll play it safe.</i>

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:54.740
<i>They can't beat Sasaki-kun for speed.</i>

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:58.460
I sure would like to answer 
one more question.

00:11:58.460 --> 00:12:00.530
<i>I shouldn't expect much help from him...</i>

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:03.110
Hey, Koshiyama-kun.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:06.410
Push my button, too.

00:12:07.220 --> 00:12:09.950
Wh-What?! I can't do that!

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:12.270
Sure you can.

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:13.080
See?

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:17.270
Like this.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:23.970
<b>Sasajima{back of her swimsuit, if wanted}</b>

00:12:29.820 --> 00:12:31.480
You can push both like this, right?

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:33.360
Oh, boy.

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:34.440
What's he doing?

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:36.400
Is that allowed?!

00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:39.250
Now that's what I call a BL buzz-in!

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:40.400
Senpai.

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:43.580
I don't know which one will light up first,

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:46.870
but if it works, you can 
be both first and second!

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:50.120
N-No... I want to do this properly...

00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:54.330
Yeah, but if he buzzes in, we lose, right?

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:58.790
Let's get the next one right 
as a pair so we can win!

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:02.010
Are they allowed to buzz that way?

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:07.250
What? Were there any rules in 
the program about how you can

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:08.990
and can't push the button?

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:13.060
I'm still holding my own buzzer, too.

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:14.560
It's not against any rules, is it?

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:19.520
<i>Do you really think you'll win the 
right to answer by buzzing that way?</i>

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:22.550
Niina, who is that kid?

00:13:22.550 --> 00:13:24.150
Since when was he on the quiz team?

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:28.490
He suddenly showed up about two weeks ago.

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:30.740
Sekigawata Middle School 
Sekigawata High School

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:34.260
I'm Sonohara, and I'm a 
third-year in middle school.

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:37.500
I want to try quiz bowl, too.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:40.090
Everyone's welcome to join this club.

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:41.460
Want to try it out?

00:13:41.720 --> 00:13:44.590
All right! Thank you!

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:50.010
But exams started right after 
that, and the club took a break,

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:53.790
so I honestly didn't have time 
to figure out what he was like.

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:58.630
Are President Sonohara and 
her brother on bad terms?

00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:00.690
He's being really provocative.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:03.570
<i>It's not as if we don't get along.</i>

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:06.150
<i>To Akira, this is just a game.</i>

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:11.190
<i>A mean-spirited game he plays only 
to rile others up and toy with them.</i>

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:14.430
If you don't do it, we'll 
lose. That okay with you?

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:15.290
But...

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:18.250
If anyone can do it, it's you.

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:22.750
I thought getting into quiz bowl and 
making friends might change him a bit,

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:24.860
but I guess that'd be too easy.

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:26.220
What should we do?

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:29.720
Very well. Continue with the question.

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:31.430
R-Right...

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:34.140
<i>I-I don't want to do it like this, but...</i>

00:14:34.730 --> 00:14:38.340
<i>I don't want to lose at this point, either!</i>

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:42.860
I have to win and face 
Mikuriya-kun in Round 3!

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:45.810
Mikuriya? A-ha...

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:47.240
Question.

00:14:49.560 --> 00:14:52.140
The commonly used kanji with 
a stroke count of o—

00:14:54.730 --> 00:14:57.000
<i>The first and second buzzed in together!</i>

00:14:57.210 --> 00:14:58.640
<i>Whose buzzers were they?!</i>

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:00.380
Th-This is...

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:05.300
...a success!

00:15:06.060 --> 00:15:10.550
The Koshiyama x Sonohara pair has 
the exclusive right to answer!

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:12.990
They really lit up both of 'em!

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:14.300
By doing it that way?!

00:15:14.670 --> 00:15:18.770
What'll be important is whether his 
first answer is correct or not.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:21.040
First, Sonohara-kun.

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:24.760
Let's see... Kanji with a stroke count of...

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:25.880
One?

00:15:26.330 --> 00:15:27.330
Correct.

00:15:27.330 --> 00:15:28.440
Oh, that was right?

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:32.160
<i>Wasn't he just reciting 
the rest of the question?</i>

00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:36.040
The second answer, Koshiyama-kun, please.

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:39.810
Commonly used kanji with only one stroke...

00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:42.130
<i>The one-stroke kanji are "ichi" and...</i>

00:15:43.190 --> 00:15:44.010
<i>"Otsu."</i>

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:45.290
Correct.

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:47.170
<b>Q: The commonly used kanji with a stroke 
count of one are what and what?  A: Ichi, otsu</b>

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:49.220
Answering correctly as a pairing 
gives them three "Right" marks.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:50.550
<b>Group</b>

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:50.550
Mouri x Ohara

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:50.550
Sonohara x 
Koshiyama

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:50.550
Sasaki x Kon

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:50.550
Mukai x Yasuura

00:15:49.220 --> 00:15:53.300
The Koshiyama x Sonohara pair 
will advance to round 3.

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:55.160
Yay!

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:58.060
Isn't quiz bowl fun, Koshiyama?

00:15:58.220 --> 00:15:59.180
<b>No honorific...</b>

00:15:58.420 --> 00:16:01.260
<i>"Koshiyama?" I'm older than you...</i>

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:02.900
Yeah...

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:09.550
What's with that expression? They lost 
because they weren't good enough.

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:12.160
Hey! It's not like your 
pair won because of you!

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:13.070
It was Koshiyama—

00:16:13.940 --> 00:16:16.910
What are you talking about? 
It was my strategy that won it.

00:16:17.960 --> 00:16:20.160
<i>He's right. If it wasn't for that idea...</i>

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:21.680
I'll buzz in.

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:23.350
Question.

00:16:24.110 --> 00:16:24.780
In th—

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:28.160
See? Like this.

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:32.550
I'm new to our club.

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:37.050
<i>Thinking of him as a beginner in quiz 
bowl, just like me, was careless.</i>

00:16:39.250 --> 00:16:42.730
<i>He looks like he's joking around, 
but his speed of thought...</i>

00:16:46.800 --> 00:16:49.650
We will now take a twenty-minute break.

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:52.410
That cringe-worthy behavior 
reminds me of someone...

00:16:52.410 --> 00:16:54.130
Why are you right there?!

00:16:54.130 --> 00:16:56.410
Something about the way it seems 
like he's mocking people...

00:16:56.750 --> 00:16:59.170
I thought he looked familiar, too.

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:01.410
Actually... I do, too.

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:04.370
<i>Could he be...</i>

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:08.880
I'm so excited for Round 3.

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:11.840
Aren't you, Lieutenant Colonel Chisato?

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:20.820
Nice goin', Shiki-kun!

00:17:20.820 --> 00:17:22.870
Congratulations, Koshiyama-kun!

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:23.570
Thanks.

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:25.850
You ended up being saved by your partner,

00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:28.330
but you did well to advance to Round 3.

00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:32.070
Let's go over the Round 3 rules 
during the twenty-minute break.

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:34.030
Okay.

00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:35.990
Sonohara.

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:38.910
I did it, President Niina!

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:43.030
I'm the only one from Sekigawata 
to advance to Round 3!

00:17:43.030 --> 00:17:44.750
I'll do my best!

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:49.960
There's something I need to say to you, 
as Sekigawata's quiz club president.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:51.650
What is it?

00:17:53.540 --> 00:17:55.270
Even if it wasn't against the rules,

00:17:55.960 --> 00:18:00.470
I can't let someone who rode roughshod 
over etiquette participate in Round 3.

00:18:03.610 --> 00:18:06.230
You can go home now.

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:18.630
Go home? That's harsh.

00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:21.510
I didn't know anything 
about quiz bowl etiquette.

00:18:22.020 --> 00:18:23.950
This concerns more than just quiz bowl.

00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:27.410
What gives you the right to take that 
attitude toward the other participants?

00:18:27.860 --> 00:18:30.030
If you're just in it for 
kicks, take it elsewhere.

00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:31.360
You're ruining it for everyone else.

00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:32.630
Hey, Niina...

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:35.460
I've never seen President Niina like this.

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:37.340
Despite appearances, he fits 
the role of club president.

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:49.520
I'm sorry... I wasn't in it just for kicks.

00:18:51.820 --> 00:18:55.570
When I'm having fun, 
I just get so wound up...

00:19:01.220 --> 00:19:02.660
Oh, now he's crying...

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:03.750
You made him cry.

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:05.700
Huh? Who... me?

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:08.870
I just wanted to be in quiz 
bowl with everyone...

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:12.150
Hey, come on... You're a middle 
school third-year! Quit crying!

00:19:12.150 --> 00:19:14.590
I just wanted to do quiz bowl...

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:17.750
Well, then, can you show 
some manners next time?

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:19.840
I can!

00:19:20.180 --> 00:19:21.050
You'd better promise.

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:24.220
Niina...

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:28.420
Tee-hee.

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:34.530
Y-You can't let him trick you like that!

00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:41.950
<i>This is a circus!</i>

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:45.240
Koshiyama! Koshiyama!

00:19:45.690 --> 00:19:46.730
Over here.

00:19:47.070 --> 00:19:49.250
Huh? Inoue, why're you over there?

00:19:49.610 --> 00:19:52.290
We figured out who that kid is!

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:53.570
Who he is?

00:19:54.990 --> 00:19:58.760
What?! Akira-kun's the girl who 
interrupted us in the arcade in Akiba?!

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:04.100
It's definitely him!

00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:06.920
He actually called Mikuriya 
"Lieutenant Colonel Chisato"!

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:07.770
I'll crush him.

00:20:08.070 --> 00:20:09.730
H-Huh?

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:14.720
What's this about Akiba and an arcade?

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:16.920
And what's "Lieutenant 
Colonel Chisato" about?

00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:18.190
Does that mean...

00:20:18.850 --> 00:20:20.900
Akira-kun's a girl?!

00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:23.860
Uh, no. Calm down, Koshiyama-kun.

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:29.080
Still, between the provocative 
attitude and the tricky tactics,

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:33.580
she—I mean, he definitely 
sees this as just a game.

00:20:39.020 --> 00:20:40.800
Hey...

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:43.660
Are you guys...

00:20:44.100 --> 00:20:45.760
actual quiz freaks?

00:20:46.490 --> 00:20:48.900
You take quiz bowl seriously, right?

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:51.370
Then...

00:20:54.530 --> 00:20:56.820
All the more reason we can't lose to him!

00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:33.490
It's time for the high school 
quiz bowl championships!

00:22:33.960 --> 00:22:38.000
All the veterans from around Japan who won 
the preliminary rounds will face off!

00:22:38.540 --> 00:22:41.500
I bet they're all crazy good.

00:22:41.970 --> 00:22:45.590
I'm sure there'll be some questions 
that even we can answer!

00:22:46.360 --> 00:22:49.510
Indeed. Let's watch it together for study!

00:22:50.750 --> 00:22:51.960
I can't wait!

00:22:52.510 --> 00:23:00.190
<b>High School Quiz Bowl Championships</b>

00:22:52.510 --> 00:23:00.190
<b>Sept. 1 (Fri.)</b>

00:22:52.510 --> 00:23:00.190
<b>Starting at 9:00 PM</b>

00:22:53.070 --> 00:22:57.460
The championships air on Friday,
 September 1st at 9:00 PM!

00:22:58.200 --> 00:22:59.680
Victory!
